From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:35:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] MAINTAINERS: use a common prefix for MM components

Several MM component entries still use standalone headings, so searching
for headings beginning with "MEMORY MANAGEMENT" misses them.

Give these 18 entries the common "MEMORY MANAGEMENT - " prefix.  Leave
them in place so the renames can be reviewed separately from the moves.
The slab allocator entry already has the prefix.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---
